  publisher = {{Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH}},
  issn = {2509-9426},
  doi = {10.1007/s41748-025-00890-x},
  abstract = {In this paper, author would like to make changes in the article title, replace revised Figure~2 and changes in the acknowledgement section as given below: Published title: Advancing Soil Moisture Prediction Using Satellite and UAV-based Imagery Using Moisture Indices with Machine Learning Models Revised title: Advancing Soil Moisture Prediction Using Satellite and UAV-based Imagery with Machine Learning Models Published Figure 2 (Figure presented.) Revised Figure 2 (Figure presented.) DJI Matrices 300 UAV (a), multispectral RedEdge-MX sensor (b), GCPs (c), and calibration panel (d) Published Acknowledgement: The authors gratefully acknowledge PSDP-funded project DDSDP staff and Center for Precision Agriculture (C4PA) staff at PMAS-Arid Agriculture University Rawalpindi (UAAR), for their continuous support throughout the execution of this research. Additionally, authors would also like to thank Dr. Muhammad Naveed Tahir, Dr. Shoaib Rashid Saleem, and Dr. Muhammad Amin for their valuable guidance and support during the project. Special thanks are also extended to Basit Shahzad and Zainab Haroon for their assistance in data collection. Revised Acknowledgement: The authors gratefully acknowledge PSDP-funded project DDSDP staff and Center for Precision Agriculture (C4PA) staff at PMAS-Arid Agriculture University Rawalpindi (UAAR), for their continuous support throughout the execution of this research. Additionally, authors would also like to thank Dr. Muhammad Naveed Tahir, Dr. Shoaib Rashid Saleem, and Dr. Muhammad Amin for their valuable guidance and support during the project. Special thanks are also extended to Basit Shahzad and Zainab Haroon for their assistance in data collection. Authors are also thankful to Dr. Fitsum T. Teshome, Dr. Haimanote K. Bayabil, and the staff of Water Resources Research Group at the University of Florida, USA, for the capacity building of Saddam Hussain. \copyright{} King Abdulaziz University and Springer Nature Switzerlan